[
    {
        "content": "<p>How and when are default instances applied? I'm trying to synthesize an instance for <code>HAdd Nat ?_ ?_</code> expecting that it will fill both mvars with <code>Nat</code> but it does not work.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- this works</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">infer_instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HAdd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- this does not, how do I enforce to use the default instance `instHAdd` ?</span>\n<span class=\"n\">run_meta</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkFreshTypeMVar</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkFreshTypeMVar</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cls</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkAppN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``HAdd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">synthInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cls</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 583021379,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1775045341
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You need to use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Elab.Term.mkInstMVar#doc\">docs#Lean.Elab.Term.mkInstMVar</a>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">run_elab</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkFreshTypeMVar</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkFreshTypeMVar</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cls</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkAppN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``HAdd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkInstMVar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cls</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">synthesizeSyntheticMVarsUsingDefault</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Actually populating the mvar is delayed though until you run <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Elab.Term.synthesizeSyntheticMVarsUsingDefault#doc\">docs#Lean.Elab.Term.synthesizeSyntheticMVarsUsingDefault</a> or <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Elab.Term.synthesizeSyntheticMVarsNoPostponing#doc\">docs#Lean.Elab.Term.synthesizeSyntheticMVarsNoPostponing</a>.<br>\nIf you are in a term elaborator, this will happen automatically eventually. If instead you are in a tactic, you'll have to do it yourself (or use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Elab.Tactic.runTermElab#doc\">docs#Lean.Elab.Tactic.runTermElab</a>).</p>",
        "id": 583022853,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1775045791
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks! Right now, I'm only in <code>MetaM</code> so I will just do</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">run_meta</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkFreshTypeMVar</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkFreshTypeMVar</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cls</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkAppN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``HAdd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">go</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TermElabM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkInstMVar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cls</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">synthesizeSyntheticMVarsUsingDefault</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">go</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{}</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
